    body = [=[
=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough Crystals to any San d'Orian {p:Conquest Overseer} to raise your Rank bar and unlock this mission, one crystal should be enough.
* Speak to any {n:Gate Guard} and accept the mission.
* Head to {z:La Theine Plateau} and speak to {n:Galaihaurat} at (E-6), at the very top of the cliffs.
** If you are already level 99, the fastest travel option is the warp to {z:Abyssea - La Theine} via {n:Horst} that puts you at at (E-4).
** Other alternatives are {p:Outpost Warp}/{p:Survival Guide} to {z:West Ronfaure} and zoning into {z:La Theine Plateau} or {z:Ordelle's Caves} {p:Survival Guide}.
* At the east side of (F-6), head down the ramp.
* Continue into {z:Ordelle's Caves} at (F-7), in a tunnel at the south of the canyon.
** **(Optional)**: You can talk to {n:Equesobillot}, {n:Deaufrain}, {n:Vicorpasse}, {n:Augevinne}, {n:Yaucevouchat}, {n:Laurisse}, and {n:Narvecaint} for some additional dialogue as you head down into and through the canyon.
* Once inside {z:Ordelle's Caves}, follow the left wall and talk to {n:Ruillont} at (G-3) in the corner behind a rock, in the small pond.
* Go back to {z:La Theine Plateau}. Either {n:Deaufrain} (halfway up the ramp out of the canyon), {n:Equesobillot} (at the top of the ramp out of the canyon) or {n:Galaihaurat} (at the top of the cliffs by a wall next to the canyon) will have the {p:Bronze Sword} needed to progress the mission.
** The NPC which has the sword seems to be entirely random for each player.
* Head back to {n:Ruillont} in {z:Ordelle's Caves}, and trade his {p:Bronze Sword} to him.
* Go back to {z:La Theine Plateau} and talk to {n:Vicorpasse} (F-6) for {@k} {k:Rescue training certificate}.
* Return to a {n:Gate Guard} to complete the mission.

=2 Notes
* A Map of {z:La Theine Plateau} and {z:Ordelle's Caves} can be purchased from the {p:Map NPCs|Map Vendor} in {z:Northern San d'Oria} and {z:Southern San d'Oria} prior to leaving town, but they are not required to progress.
* If instead of the mission's normal dialogue, most involved NPCs state __"The suspect appears to have taken refuge within Ordelle's Caves. We will follow our training drills and stick to our posts!"__, then you have a conflicting quest active, {q:A Timely Visit|A Timely Visit|A Timely Visit}.
** You're not required to complete this quest to progress, but some NPCs may require talking to more than once for their mission-specific dialogue.
* If you somehow drop or otherwise lose the sword given to you during the mission, you'll need to acquire a new {p:Bronze Sword} from somewhere else to progress.
** The NPC who was keeping it will say __"Didn't I give you his sword? Just hand it to Ruillont. Don't you lose it!"__ and does not appear to be able to miraculously give you another one, even if you zone after losing it.

